Subject: [core] TESTNET-ONLY — expose getCCIPAdmin()/setCCIPAdmin() on wstETH

Base: lib/core @ fe5aa4956 (lidofinance/core, feat/scratch-dg)
Applies to: contracts/0.6.12/WstETH.sol

WHY
  CCIP's TokenAdminRegistry is registered into permissionlessly, but only via one of the
  conventions RegistryModuleOwnerCustom knows: getCCIPAdmin(), owner(), or AccessControl's
  DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE. The disposable Lido core that step 01 deploys to Sepolia carries the
  canonical WstETH, which exposes NONE of them — so without this the deployer cannot seat
  itself as TAR admin and step 07 falls into its guarded impersonation branch, which aborts
  on a live RPC (script/07_set_pool_gov.sh:155-171).

  Adding the hook (mirroring Chainlink's own BurnMintERC20) makes step 07 run
  impersonation-free against the REAL Chainlink Sepolia TAR. See LIVE_DEPLOY_CONCERNS.md
  §1 and §5 item 3.

SCOPE — DO NOT GENERALISE
  This changes deployed bytecode and is valid ONLY for the throwaway testnet core. Canonical
  mainnet wstETH is immutable and cannot gain this hook, so mainnet CCIP onboarding still
  requires the TAR owner (Chainlink) to seat the admin manually. Treat that as a real
  onboarding dependency, not something this patch solves.

diff --git a/contracts/0.6.12/WstETH.sol b/contracts/0.6.12/WstETH.sol
index 0f3620abe..217ee54f7 100644
--- a/contracts/0.6.12/WstETH.sol
+++ b/contracts/0.6.12/WstETH.sol
@@ -28,6 +28,17 @@ import "./interfaces/IStETH.sol";
 contract WstETH is ERC20Permit {
     IStETH public stETH;
 
+    /// @dev TESTNET-ONLY ADDITION (wsteth-2.0): CCIP TokenAdminRegistry admin hook. Canonical
+    /// mainnet wstETH is immutable and exposes neither this nor Ownable/AccessControl, so on
+    /// mainnet CCIP onboarding requires the TAR owner (Chainlink) to seat the admin. Adding
+    /// `getCCIPAdmin()` here lets the disposable/testnet wstETH self-register into CCIP's
+    /// TokenAdminRegistry via RegistryModuleOwnerCustom.registerAdminViaGetCCIPAdmin — no
+    /// owner-impersonation needed. Seeded to the deployer (constructor msg.sender) at deploy.
+    /// See LIVE_DEPLOY_CONCERNS.md §1-§2.
+    address private s_ccipAdmin;
+
+    event CCIPAdminTransferred(address indexed previousAdmin, address indexed newAdmin);
+
     /**
      * @param _stETH address of the StETH token to wrap
      */
@@ -37,6 +48,23 @@ contract WstETH is ERC20Permit {
         ERC20("Wrapped liquid staked Ether 2.0", "wstETH")
     {
         stETH = _stETH;
+        s_ccipAdmin = msg.sender;
+        emit CCIPAdminTransferred(address(0), msg.sender);
+    }
+
+    /// @notice Returns the CCIP administrator, as read by CCIP's
+    ///         RegistryModuleOwnerCustom.registerAdminViaGetCCIPAdmin(token).
+    function getCCIPAdmin() external view returns (address) {
+        return s_ccipAdmin;
+    }
+
+    /// @notice Transfers the CCIP administrator. Restricted to the current CCIP admin.
+    /// @param newAdmin the new CCIP administrator.
+    function setCCIPAdmin(address newAdmin) external {
+        require(msg.sender == s_ccipAdmin, "wstETH: not CCIP admin");
+        address previousAdmin = s_ccipAdmin;
+        s_ccipAdmin = newAdmin;
+        emit CCIPAdminTransferred(previousAdmin, newAdmin);
     }
 
     /**
